==Malay==

===Etymology 1===
Phonetic spelling of {{m|ms|-kah}} in a Johor-Riau accent.

====Pronunciation====
{{ms-IPA}}

====Conjunction====
{{ms-conj|j=ک}}

# {{lb|ms|informal}} [[or]]
#: {{syn|ms|atau}}
#: {{ux|ms|Besar '''ke''' kecil?|Big '''or''' small?}}
#: {{ux|ms|Boleh '''ke''' tak?|Can you do it ('''or''' not)?}}

====Suffix====
{{ms-suffix|j=ک}}

# {{lb|ms|informal}} used on [[modal verb]]s, [[adverbs]], [[verb]]s and [[noun]]s to form [[question]]s
#: {{usex|ms|Boleh '''ke''' aku pinjam fon kau?|Can I borrow your phone?}}
#: {{usex|ms|Selalu '''ke''' cikgu tanya soalan macam tu?|Is it often that the teacher ask questions like that?}}
#: {{usex|ms|Abang kau dah beli '''ke''' PS5 yang dia kata nak beli tu?|Has your brother bought the PS5 that he said he was going to buy?}}
#: {{usex|ms|Kau '''ke''' yang dapat markah 100% dekat ujian baru-baru ni tu?|Are you the one that got a score of a 100% for the recent test?}}

=====Usage notes=====
Note that unlike {{m|ms|-kah}}, {{m|ms|ke}} isn't written conjoined with a preceding word.

